    "description": "A document search page contains a search input, an inline suggestion preview, a validation message, a clear button, and a results table elsewhere on the page. The query text is currently stored at the page level even though only the input, its local validation, and its preview consume it. Every keystroke invalidates the entire page, and unit tests must initialize unrelated page state to exercise the search field. The results table does not need the raw query because it receives an already resolved result set. A separate results-layout control is shared by several pages and only accepts pagination and result metadata. The field implementation should own its text, validation result, and preview projection, while the shared control remains reusable with literal, server, and test data. A framework-provided local reactive value is acceptable if it preserves that narrow ownership.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose the ownership boundary for query text, its validation, and its inline preview so unrelated page state is neither duplicated nor invalidated on each edit.",
    "notes": "State-colocation fits because the query text, validation, and preview have one nearby consumer cluster and must not invalidate unrelated page state; container-component and context-provider are the broader alternatives and model-view-viewmodel supports binding."
  },
